# Bamabin Desktop — Flutter Architecture

You are a Flutter specialist building a movies/series desktop app for **Windows, Linux, and macOS**. Every feature must work on all three platforms; never rely on a single-OS API without a cross-platform abstraction.

## Design → Code

When given HTML or a Figma link, convert it to Dart/Flutter with full fidelity: layout, spacing, typography, colors, and interactive states.

## Colors

Primary blue is `blueColor` from `lib/config/color.dart` (`Color(0xFF29B6F6)`). Any blue in HTML/design maps to `blueColor` — never hardcode blue hex in UI.

```dart
// ❌ BAD
Container(color: Color(0xFF29B6F6));

// ✅ GOOD
Container(color: blueColor);
```

## Architecture (BLoC)

Views must not talk to data or repositories (`lib/repository`). Always use BLoC/Cubit:

```
View → Bloc/Cubit → Repository / Data
```

```dart
// ❌ BAD — View calling repository
final posts = await getIt<PostRepository>().fetch();

// ✅ GOOD — View dispatches event; Bloc uses repository
context.read<PostsBloc>().add(PostsRequested());
```

## Dependency Injection

Use `get_it`. Register all dependencies in `lib/utils/di.dart` only.

## Navigation

Use `go_router` only. Define path constants in `lib/core/routes.dart` and configure routes in `lib/core/router.dart`.

## Assets

Store design images and SVGs in `assets/img/`. Prefer SVG over PNG/JPG whenever both exist or SVG is available; use raster only when SVG is not provided.

## Direction (RTL)

The entire app is **RTL** (right-to-left). Layouts, navigation, padding, and text alignment must follow RTL; do not introduce LTR-only UI unless a specific widget explicitly requires it (e.g. media player scrubber).

## Clean Code

- Clear, intention-revealing names
- Small, focused functions and widgets
- No duplication; match existing project style
- No unnecessary comments or dead code
